From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Market Canopy <office@marketcanopy.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Market Canopy as the AI agent's managed provider; no
 run_script or stdio MCP

ADR 0525, amended 2026-10-26: the managed provider "marketcanopy" is the
AI agent's default, and people may also add upstream's providers with
their own keys. Its code is in the overlay (src/providers/marketcanopy);
this change wires it in. The registry offers it beside upstream's
providers. main.tsx imports the bootstrap, which puts it first in the
stored settings before the stores load, and the watcher, which cancels
requests in flight and reloads the models when the account or
organization changes. The settings page shows the Market Canopy
connection above the person's own providers; the provider list and the
Add provider dialog leave it out, since it needs no URL or key. Saved
MCP settings keep only URL servers. Web search is upstream's, with each
person's own Exa key.

Native code no longer runs processes for the agent: run_script is not
registered, and the renderer's _createProcess, which started stdio MCP
servers, refuses every call. file_opener's description stops pointing at
run_script.

A plugin in the user folder with the GUID of a bundled AI plugin (the
agent or the in-editor AI plugin) and a higher version no longer
replaces the bundled one, so a plugin from the store cannot drop the
Market Canopy provider.
